jawas is a backup tool for databases, in the spirit of automysqlbackup:
one compressed dump per database, rotated in daily, weekly and monthly
series.

- engines: MySQL and MariaDB (mysqldump), PostgreSQL (pg_dump, plain or
  custom format, plus roles through pg_dumpall), SQLite (consistent hot
  copy or SQL dump); several servers in one configuration
- weekly and monthly copies are hard links of the daily dump; retention
  in days per period with a keep_min floor
- streaming compression: gzip, pigz, bzip2, xz or zstd
- atomic writes, SHA-256 sidecar files, 0600 files, no clear-text
  password in the configuration nor on the command line
- dry-run by default (--apply to act), lock, pre/post hooks, JSON report
  and monitoring-friendly exit codes
